@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title The TUI stack — Bubble Tea v2, the versions proveo builds against, and what the proxy asks of a Program
' purpose: which TUI library draws proveo's prompts, at which versions, and why those versions are pinned by a test
' covers: go.mod (the charm.land requirements)
' covers: internal/contract/tui_stack_pins_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/tea_envmsg_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/tui_ratchets_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/screen.go, internal/choiceui/screen_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/frames_test.go, internal/choiceui/form_model_test.go
' covers: e2e/form_tty_test.go
'   what the spikes measured ......... _spec/_experiments/terminal-handoff-probes.puml (THE PORT)
'   the decisions, D3 D8 D9 .......... _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml (DECISIONS)
'   the order the port lands in ...... _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml (W4, W5, W9, W10)
'   who owns the terminal ............ _spec/internal/ptyproxy/pty-ownership.puml
'   what sbx's own TUI looks like .... _spec/_experiments/sbx-tui-observed.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
' This file grows as the port lands. Landed so far, all 2026-11-10: B0 (the
' pins), B2 (the proxy hosts a Program), B3 (the Ctrl+C dialog), B4 and B5
' (the tcell overlay and modal are deleted). On 2026-11-11: B11, B6, B7 and
' W-e (the forms), then B8 and B9 (the pickers; the old libraries left).
'
' ── WHY BUBBLE TEA v2 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' THE STACK WAS NOT THE CAUSE of the three measured defects; none needed a
' framework change. The recommendation was to stay on tcell while they were
' fixed. D3 ports anyway.
' The Executor, 2026-11-10: "Port everything to Bubble Tea v2" (D3), and for
' the drawing: "Rewrite the views in lipgloss" (D9). The stated reference is
' sbx's own TUI. MEASURED with `go version -m` on sbx 0.50.0: it embeds
' bubbletea v2.0.10, bubbles v2.2.1 and lipgloss v2.0.6.
' No proveo file imports tcell since the forms moved (W9). Both libraries
' left go.mod on 2026-11-11 (W10, B9): _spec/internal/choiceui/scope-tree.puml.
'
' ── THE PINS (B0) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   charm.land/bubbletea/v2  v2.1.1
'   charm.land/bubbles/v2    v2.2.1
'   charm.land/lipgloss/v2   v2.1.0
' EXPLICIT VERSIONS, NEVER @latest. MEASURED: `go get …@latest` moved the go
' directive and switched the toolchain without a word. lipgloss v2.1.0 needs
' go 1.26.7, which is why go.mod's directive reads `go 1.26.7` and the
' toolchain pin moved to 1.26.10 first (toolchain-provisioning.puml). The
' Executor chose that over pinning lipgloss v2.0.6: "Bump Go to 1.26.7+".
' WHAT THE PINS DRAGGED ALONG, MEASURED from `go get`'s own output:
'   upgraded  go-runewidth v0.0.16 -> v0.0.30 (a direct dependency: ui and
'             choiceui measure text with it), go-colorful v1.2.0 -> v1.4.1,
'             golang.org/x/sys v0.46.0 -> v0.47.0, x/sync v0.13.0 -> v0.22.0
'   added     ultraviolet (an untagged pseudo-version), colorprofile,
'             x/ansi, x/term, x/termios, x/windows, displaywidth, uax29,
'             cancelreader v0.2.2, xo/terminfo
' The unit suites of ui, choiceui, ptyproxy, agentio and cmd/proveo passed
' under the upgraded width library, and all eight release targets still build.
' [Inference] No visible width changed. The suites compare rendered text; no
' terminal was looked at for this.
' bubbles is pinned ahead of its first import, so go.mod marks it indirect
' and `go mod tidy` would drop it. go.mod was not tidy before this either
' (tidy also removes martian and x/net); only the three modules proveo now
' imports were moved to the direct block, by hand.
' A TEST HOLDS THE PINS, because a later `go get` of any Charm module can move
' all three. It checks the resolved build list and the literal go.mod lines.
'
' ── THE FIRST SURFACE: THE CTRL+C DIALOG (B2, B3) ──────────────────────────
' How the proxy hosts a Program, and why it decodes the keys itself:
' _spec/internal/ptyproxy/pty-ownership.puml (THE OVERLAY HOSTS A BUBBLE TEA
' PROGRAM). What this file keeps is the part every later surface repeats.
' A VIEW IS REWRITTEN, AND HELD TO THE RENDERER IT REPLACES. typedModal
' (modal_tea.go) is the typed-answer confirm as a model; its view is lipgloss:
' a NormalBorder in the warning colour, padding 0 x 2, one styled string per
' row, placed with lipgloss.Place. A test draws the tcell dialog on a
' simulation screen and compares the two as plain text, cell for cell, at
' five sizes, three inputs and two dialogs. They are equal.
' THAT COMPARISON WAS THE GATE, AND IT IS GONE WITH BOTH SIDES. One wave
' later the typed dialog became a button row
' (_spec/internal/choiceui/confirm-dialogs.puml) and the tcell modal was
' deleted (B5), so neither renderer of the comparison exists any more. The
' forms' port was held to golden frames instead: THE FORMS, below.
' NO MESSAGE REACHES A FORMATTER. tea.EnvMsg carries the whole environment,
' and a spike that logged its messages wrote the operator's variables to a
' file. A contract test parses every Go file that imports bubbletea and fails
' on: a tea.Msg parameter passed to any call but a model's Update, the name
' tea.EnvMsg, and tea.LogToFile.
' [Inference] The check is syntactic. A message copied into another variable
' and formatted there passes it.
'
' ── THE FORMS (B11, B6, B7, W-e) — 2026-11-11 ──────────────────────────────
' THE ORACLE CAME FIRST (B11, 6fe4a3e2). frames_test.go draws every form,
' page and topology state at the sizes viewport.puml names and compares each
' frame's plain text with a file: 131 under internal/choiceui/testdata/frames/.
' The tcell renderer wrote them, and they were committed before any drawing
' changed. PROVEO_UPDATE_FRAMES=1 rewrites them.
' THE DRAWING KEEPS ITS GEOMETRY (B6, B7, e9b719df). draw() still places text
' by column and row. What changed is the sink. screen (screen.go) collects
' styled runs; view() turns each run into one lipgloss Layer at its x and y
' with a rising Z, composed on a Canvas of the terminal's size. A later run
' covers an earlier one, which is what a cell grid did.
' MEASURED: the port's first run equalled all 131 golden frames.
' THIS IS NARROWER THAN THE PLAN'S READING OF D9. The plan had about 890
' lines of drawing rewritten and the positional tests replaced by the
' goldens. The port kept draw(), canvas and pen, retargeted at screen, and
' kept the positional tests through a shim (screen_test.go renders a frame
' and reads it back by cell).
' [Inference] D9 ("Rewrite the views in lipgloss") may have meant flow layout
' (JoinVertical, Place). The topology strip and the viewport budget are column
' arithmetic; a flow rewrite would move frames the goldens hold fixed. The
' Executor has not confirmed this reading.
' B6 WAS NEVER DEAD CODE. The plan built the views beside the old drawing and
' wired them in B7. With one sink swapped under an unchanged draw() there was
' no second view to build, so B6 and B7 are one commit.
' THE EVENT LOOP IS A MODEL. formModel holds the form, the cursor, the tick
' and the size. A tea.KeyPressMsg becomes a press: a named key ("enter",
' "shift+tab") or typed text. Form.key applies it and reports an Outcome when
' the form ends. The figure's clock: _spec/internal/choiceui/topology-strip.puml.
' THE FORM OPENS /dev/tty ITSELF. tcell wrote to /dev/tty. A Program writes to
' stdout unless told otherwise, so `proveo run x >/dev/null` would have drawn
' nothing. RunStep hands openTerminal()'s file to the Program as input and
' output. MEASURED on tmux by e2e/form_tty_test.go: the form draws, takes a
' key and leaves on Esc with stdout on /dev/null.
' THE LOCALE REWRITE IS GONE. Under LANG=C tcell encoded private-use glyphs
' as '?', so Run() rewrote POSIX locales to C.UTF-8. The rewrite left with
' tcell.
' [Unverified] That a LANG=C terminal shows the glyphs now. No run under
' LANG=C was looked at.
' ONE PALETTE. The dialogs carried a lipgloss palette beside the forms' tcell
' one. Both read styles() now. The two-tone key line it gained:
' _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml.
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/frames_test.go: TestFramesMatchTheGoldenFiles
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/form_model_test.go:
'   TestTheFormsKeysMeanWhatTheyMeantOnTcell
'   TestArrowsMoveTheCursorAndChangeTheAnswer
'   TestTypingGoesToAFieldAndNotToTheForm
'   TestTheFigureMovesOnTheClockAndTheFormDrawsOnTheAlternateScreen
'   TestATerminalTooSmallTakesOnlyTheKeysThatLeave
' Pinned by e2e/form_tty_test.go:
'   TestTheRunFormDrawsOnTheTerminalWhenStdoutIsRedirected
'
' ── THE OLD LIBRARIES STAY OUT (G4, then B9) ───────────────────────────────
' While the port ran, a contract test listed every file that imported tcell
' or go-fuzzyfinder: 34 and 5 when it landed, 18 and 5 after W5 deleted the
' overlay and the modal, 0 and 5 after W9. A file outside the list failed
' it; so did a listed file that had stopped importing, which kept the list
' exact while it shrank.
' W10 moved the last five and removed both modules. The test now fails on
' any import, and any go.mod line, that names tcell, go-fuzzyfinder or
' termbox-go.
' The same file holds G5: a row in the glyph ban's exemption list whose file
' is gone, or holds no banned rune any more, fails.
' Pinned by internal/contract/tui_ratchets_test.go:
'   TestTheRetiredTUILibrariesStayOut
'   TestEveryGlyphBanExemptionStillShieldsABannedRune
'
' Pinned by internal/contract/tea_envmsg_test.go:
'   TestNoSourceFormatsABubbleTeaMessage
'   TestTheMessageLeakCheckSeesEachWayOut
'
' Pinned by internal/contract/tui_stack_pins_test.go:
'   TestTheTUIStackResolvesToItsPinnedVersions
'   TestGoModNamesTheTUIStackVersionsExplicitly

component "go.mod\nthree explicit versions" as MOD <<app>>
component "the contract test\nresolved list + literal lines" as PIN <<app>>
component """go get …@latest""\n**moves the toolchain silently**" as DRIFT <<error>>
component "bubbletea v2.1.1\nthe event loop" as TEA <<cloud>>
component "lipgloss v2.1.0\nthe drawing · needs go 1.26.7" as LIP <<cloud>>
component "bubbles v2.2.1\ntree · textinput · viewport · list" as BUB <<cloud>>
component "a rewritten view\nlipgloss, compared with tcell's cells" as VIEW <<app>>
component "screen\nstyled runs, one lipgloss layer each" as SCR <<app>>
component "131 golden frames\nwritten by the tcell renderer" as GOLD <<app>>
component "tea.EnvMsg\n**the whole environment**" as ENV <<error>>

MOD ARROW_MAIN TEA
MOD ARROW_MAIN LIP
MOD ARROW_MAIN BUB
PIN ARROW_MAIN MOD : holds
DRIFT ARROW_ERROR MOD : what the test refuses
LIP ARROW_MAIN VIEW
LIP ARROW_MAIN SCR
GOLD ARROW_MAIN SCR : holds every frame
TEA ARROW_ERROR ENV : sent to every model

note bottom of PIN
  **Three modules move together.** A ""go get""
  of one Charm module can raise the other
  two. The test names all three versions, so
  a drift fails before it ships.
end note

note bottom of LIP
  **The one that set the toolchain.** v2.1.0
  needs go 1.26.7. The Executor chose the
  bump over an older lipgloss, so go.mod and
  mise.toml moved to 1.26.10 first.
end note

note bottom of VIEW
  **Rewritten, then compared.** The lipgloss
  dialog and the tcell dialog were drawn side
  by side in a test and agreed cell for cell
  before the old renderer went.
end note

note bottom of SCR
  **The sink changed, the geometry did not.**
  The form still places text by column and
  row. Each run becomes a layer; a later one
  covers an earlier one, as cells did.
end note

note bottom of GOLD
  **Written before the port.** Every form, page
  and figure state at each named size, as
  plain text. The port's first run equalled
  all 131.
end note

note bottom of ENV
  **Never formatted.** A model may pass a
  message to another model's Update and
  nowhere else. A contract test reads every
  file that imports bubbletea for it.
end note

note bottom of BUB
  **No form, radio, checkbox or button.**
  bubbles ships none of the four. proveo's
  form and its button row stay proveo's own
  models, drawn with lipgloss.
end note
@enduml
